  {
   "id": "gittin.70a.19",
   "daf": "70a",
   "sentenceId": 18,
   "he": "שְׁלֹשָׁה דְּבָרִים מַכְחִישִׁים כֹּחוֹ שֶׁל אָדָם, וְאֵלּוּ הֵן: פַּחַד, דֶּרֶךְ וְעָוֹן. פַּחַד – דִּכְתִיב: ״לִבִּי סְחַרְחַר עֲזָבַנִי כֹחִי״. דֶּרֶךְ – דִּכְתִיב: ״עִנָּה בַדֶּרֶךְ כֹּחִי״. עָוֹן – דִּכְתִיב: ״כָּשַׁל בַּעֲוֹנִי כֹחִי״.",
   "en": "§ «Three things diminish a person’s strength, and they are: Fear,» traveling on the «road, and sin.» The Gemara explains: «Fear, as it is written: “My heart flutters, my strength fails me”» (Psalms 38:11). Traveling on the «road, as it is written: “He has weakened my strength on the road”» (Psalms 102:24). «Sin, as it is written: “My strength fails because of my sin”» (Psalms 31:11)."
  }
 ],
